From 6bd42c14f450af9bfcd36b605b1836e57d310fdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:29:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(kernel): heal seam op and solidcore native-format
 importer corpus

M12.1 stage 3 of the retirement gate. The Kernel seam gains heal():
solidcore runs the port's api_heal_brep and the seam judges the result
(empty and non-positive-tolerance input refused up front; integrity,
closed manifold, positive measure and a vertex-edge gap under
HEAL_GAP_LIMIT afterwards); truck answers Unsupported. New
solidcore_import module: the port's native ASCII B-rep format as
write_smb / read_smb / import_smb (read, heal, check).

Bench: heal and the native round trip hold five fixtures to their
closed forms; a vertex-gap fixture shows the port heals any gap by
growing tolerance, so the seam caps it; a 21-file corrupt corpus, every
case under a 60 s time bound, pins raw-reader and importer verdicts.
Findings pinned: the raw reader returns Ok-empty for garbage files and
Ok for a 1.0 vertex gap; the importer refuses all of them.

No production path switched; truck keeps its kernel role.

Refs #27

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
